## Overview
End‑to‑end system that predicts individual medical insurance premiums using a Random Forest regressor. Includes data preprocessing, model benchmarking, and a Streamlit dashboard for interactive premium calculation and cost‑driver analysis.

## Key Insights
- 🚬 Smoking accounts for ~49% of premium determination (≈$15k surcharge)
- 📊 BMI >30 adds a tiered surcharge, up to $35k–$50k for obese smokers
- 🎂 Age adds $250‑$300 per year after 25

## Features
- 💻 Robust preprocessing pipeline (`src/data_preprocessing.py`)
- 📊 Model benchmarking (Linear, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting) with R² ≈ 89.9%
- 📈 Interactive Streamlit UI (`app.py`) with premium calculator, cost‑driver waterfalls, and EDA visualisations
- 💾 Model persistence (`models/best_model.pkl`)

## How to Run Locally
```bash
cd 30-Machine-Learning-InsurancePremium
pip install -r requirements.txt
python src/train.py   # trains and saves the best model
streamlit run app.py   # launches the dashboard
```
